      "llmx IQ4_NL keeps original F32 activations under auto/f16; mx uses its default quantized CPU arithmetic. This is default-runtime comparison, not arithmetic equivalence.",
      "Candidate is the existing tested dirty development binary; mx is a clean separately pinned build using the same MSVC version/AVX2 feature set. No main-before exists for unsupported IQ4_NL.",
      "All eight calls and activity retained, no filtering/replacement, no reference parity or release verdict.",
      "All calls flag unrelated CPU and unknown process observations; cpptools consistently consumes about one logical CPU. No sample was removed.",
      "The monitor intervals span call boundaries and include process loading/warmup, so activity counts can overlap adjacent calls.",
      "Only two samples per arm and one timed repetition per child; no layout control or statistical confidence interval."
